INT. SUBMARINE MUSEUM - TORPEDO ROOM - WRESTLING MAT - NIGHT

The torpedo room of a decommissioned Cold War submarine, converted into a practice space. Rusted racks line the walls. A blue wrestling mat covers the deck plates. Pipes sweat overhead; a green emergency bulb throws everything into the color of pond water.

A faded banner: "HARBOR DISTRICT WRESTLING - STATE TRIALS."

COACH BASIL MWANGI (50s, squat, bald, whistle on a bootlace) paces the edge of the mat. He holds a stopwatch and a coffee thermos, and uses neither.

DMITRI VOLKOV (17, heavy shoulders, scarred eyebrow) crouches on the mat, rolling his neck. HECTOR LEÓN-ABARA (17, wiry, taped fingers) shakes out his arms in the opposite corner. EDDIE PRAGER (30s, local ref, striped shirt, reading glasses on a cord) squats between them to inspect their singlets.

BASIL
Last round of the night. Winner goes to State.

DMITRI
Coach, we've wrestled forty times.

BASIL
This is the forty-first.

HECTOR
He always gets the underhook.

BASIL
Then you break it.

DMITRI
He won't.

HECTOR
I will.

BASIL
Boys.

EDDIE
Gentlemen. Hands.

They touch hands. Both are damp.

EDDIE (CONT'D)
Wrestle.

They lock up. Dmitri drives. Hector sprawls. The mat squeaks.

BASIL
Hips, Hector!

DMITRI
(grunting)
Get off me.

HECTOR
Get off me!

EDDIE
Both of you, break!

They break. Circle. Dmitri shoots a double. Hector hops back, drops his weight, and rides Dmitri to the mat.

BASIL
That's it!

EDDIE
Two points, León-Abara.

DMITRI
That was a stall!

EDDIE
It was not.

BASIL
It was beautiful.

DMITRI
Coach, whose side are you on?

BASIL
Both. Neither. Wrestling.

Dmitri spits on the mat. Hector smirks. Eddie raises a warning finger.

EDDIE
One more of that, Volkov, and it's a penalty.

DMITRI
He's baiting me.

HECTOR
He's tired.

BASIL
They're both tired. Wrestle!

They lock up again. The green bulb flickers. Dmitri snaps a headlock. Hector twists. For a moment they are one tangled shape.

EDDIE
Pin, pin, hold it--

BASIL
Get your shoulders up, Hector!

HECTOR
(through his teeth)
I'm trying!

DMITRI
(through his teeth)
Stay down!

The pipes overhead groan. A drop of condensation splashes onto Eddie's glasses. He wipes it, never taking his eyes from the mat.

EDDIE
One. Two.

Hector bridges. His neck veins strain. Dmitri leans harder.

BASIL
Coach says up, Hector, up!

HECTOR
Coach says what?

BASIL
UP!

Hector explodes. He throws a hip, rolls, and lands on top of Dmitri with a crash that shakes the deck plates. Dmitri's shoulders hit the mat.

EDDIE
One. Two. Three!

He slaps the mat. Hector rolls away, chest heaving. Dmitri lies face up, staring at the pipes.

EDDIE (CONT'D)
Winner, León-Abara.

Silence. Basil sets down the thermos. Walks onto the mat and kneels beside Dmitri.

BASIL
You okay, Volkov?

DMITRI
(flat)
Fine.

BASIL
You wrestled well.

DMITRI
I lost.

BASIL
Both of those things are true.

Dmitri sits up. Hector offers a hand. Dmitri looks at it for a long beat. Takes it.

DMITRI
(quietly)
Take it to State.

HECTOR
I will.

DMITRI
And break his underhook.

Hector grins. Eddie checks his stopwatch and folds his glasses.

EDDIE
I'm going home.

BASIL
Coffee, Eddie?

EDDIE
God, yes.

The green bulb buzzes. Somewhere deep in the sub, a drip keeps time.
